A||N||17||Faz||Where's your Car? Mine has been stolen!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Faz||07-25-2001||08:14 PM||||Hello All,<P>I just bought my Fiero three weeks ago. It was an 86 GT, I got it very cheap ($250), but it needed alot of work. I spent ~$3700 to make it run (new engine, frt&rear end, assorted stuff, cut polish), and now its gone... The insurance company will not give me anything for 30 days... I wonder what they will give me. The people here at work say I'm screwed b/c its old, even if I do have reciepts. I live in Calgary, Alberta, Canada but just moved to Edmonton to take this new job. Does anyone have any idea what will probably happen (this has never happened to me). I have a feeling that the insurance company will give me almost nothing for the car (I hope they find it, but I doubt it... I'm an auditor.. therefore very sinical). <P>Sorry for jumping around, Im upset. What I want to know is:<P>#1. What will the insurance company probably give me (Canadian insurance companies pay black book value)?<P>#2. If you will forgive me for making my first post on this website so depressing... <P>#3. Do you have any advice?||||reg||8
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||07-25-2001||08:30 PM||||Holy crap!! <P>I wish I had some advice to give you, but it hasn't happened to me (knock on wood... twice...)<P>One of the regulars here just went through this in the US, though, and the other guys here in his area kept an eye out for it.... if you could give a description of the car (like any specific details that may make it more identifiable) and the VIN number, I bet there's guys in your neck of the woods that would love to pound a car thief into a smear on the pavement for you... <P>Good luck, and let us know what we can do to help....||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBert||07-25-2001||09:35 PM||||Faz - sorry to hear about your loss, believe me I can relate.  My 86GT was stolen last Friday and recovered just yesterday with wheels and stereo removed.  I can't quite help with what the insurance company will do but I will keep you posted cause I will go thru it first.<P>Yes they will make you wait for 30 days to see if it can be found.  I'm still not sure it was a good thing that mine was found.<P>I have the same fear that they will not offer me even close to what I have lost.  They may total it out and I am not sure of all the ramifications of that.  Anyway I will keep in touch with what my insurance company does and let you know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||07-25-2001||10:06 PM||||My sympathies.<P>My friends old crappy mx-6 5spd was stolen in Halifax a few years ago, they found it after 2 weeks, no damage at all except a razor slashed passenger sunvisor (why???!) , nothing stolen at all (cd player and wallets cc's etc under the seat)<P>Just a very mild joyride i guess. (for a 4cyl that car had balls)||||reg||1
Z||000004||GodSend||07-25-2001||10:41 PM||||You might be in luck.  A friend of mine was just in a write-off accident in his 1990 sunbird (near toronto).  The insurance agent took a look at the going value for a car in his condition, same model, same year.<P>Get your insurance company to check out  <A HREF="http://www.trader.ca" TARGET=_blank>http://www.trader.ca</A> , and maybe they will give you cost to replace your GT.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Robert||07-26-2001||07:29 PM||||After restoring my 87GT I asked my insurance carrier (USAA) to change my policy to a daily driver.  When they gave me the rate, I asked them what they based it on.  The said they had charts and graphs.  I countered with I had just put 5 grand into the car and if anything happened to the car I wanted to get the money back.  They told me as long as I had receipts, they would cover me.  I then asked what would happen if I decided to put a $20,000 kit on it?  They said I would need an attachment to the policy for something that large.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">   <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."||||reg||10
Z||000006||moonie||07-27-2001||08:37 PM||||i live in memphis tn.<BR>every night i go outside & take off my <BR>coil wire.<BR>while there aren't many fiero's in memphis , <BR>its still a 80's GM car.<BR>takes about 10 seconds to pop the column <BR>& be gone.<BR>as i regret what happened to you....<BR>this advice may help others<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-28-2001||10:49 AM||||That's the type of stuff that makes me want to stay in SD....||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay||07-28-2001||10:57 AM||||Faz, sorry to here about that.  They will make you wait to see if it is found.  The best thing to do is get an appraisal (too late now I guess) but Canadian companies must give you the appraised value for your car.  I only paid $500 for my GT but now it has a Northstar, so I want to make sure that the insurance company will pay me for all the work in it not just the $500 I paid for it or the wholesale value of the car.  If you have photos and reciepts this will help greatly.  I suggest that in the future you let your agent take pictures of your car and keep them on file.  Hope you don't get ripped off and don't be afraid to challenge the Insurance company if you are not satisfied with the settlement thay offer.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Faz||07-30-2001||02:04 PM||||Hi folks,<P>I have been on the public transit system ever since this has happened to me... since I waste soooo much time on the bus, this is the first chance I've had to respond to all of the advice I have recieved. I will keep you updated on what happens with my dilemma. Thanks for the advice, I will use it. I have a great pic of my car (soon after the polish) that shows the interior and exterior (no rips, and beautiful). I'm sure that'll help. I hope they give me enough to buy another fiero... I liked that car...<P>Thanks again, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Faz ||||reg||1
Z||000010||loafer87gt||07-30-2001||02:17 PM||||Hi Faz,<P>The best thing you can do is to go on to Autotrader and print out several for sale signs for Fieros that are similar to yours. Hang onto all your receipts and present them to the adjuster as well, and if you have any photos of your car show them. When my 87GT  was stolen the first time they wanted to write it off and give me $1700, and it was in near perfect condition before the theft. After I showed them that similar cars were selling for 5-6000 CNDN, and showed them all my photos I had taken just a week before the theft, along with my stack of receipts, they realized that the 1700 number was unrealistic. Don't take their first offer, it will take along time, and will feel like your pushing a rope, but you should reach some sort of agreement with your insurance guys if you hash it out long enough. After they looked at the numbers, they just decided it wasn't worth writing off my car, and decided to do repairs to it instead. This was my experience with the Saskatchewan auto insurance guys anyways.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Faz||09-10-2001||07:57 PM||||Hello folks,<P>The insurance company settled with me today. It wasn't bad, I received 5,700.00 for the car plus they paid for my rental (one month). Either way, Thanks for all of the help, and I look forward to driving a fiero again soon. <P>-Faz||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||09-10-2001||08:04 PM||||Damn, sounds like you made out like a bandit.<P>See, it was a blessing in disguise...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||09-10-2001||08:49 PM||||Faz,<P>Sounds good. Gonna get another one?<BR>Don't be a stranger.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
